exports[`report a narrated take 1`] = `
"# Checkout total

0:31 screen recording · 10 keyframes · 7 spoken lines · 1 error captured · recorded 2026-10-15 14:02 · http://localhost:4810

**This walkthrough:** \`https://handback.example/w/s1\`

A person recorded this while using the app, talking through what they saw: a bug, review notes, or a change they want. The narration says what they meant; the frames show what was on screen. When the two disagree, trust the frames. The words were transcribed by Whisper large-v3 (Groq). The speaker didn't read them back, so names, units and small numbers are the likeliest to be wrong.

Every path is relative to this walkthrough's files (the paths inside the folder if you downloaded it). Times are positions on one clock from the start; the \`mmss\` inside a frame's filename is time inside that take's own video, so the two can differ.

## Start here

The 4 of 10 frames that carry the most evidence, in time order (★ in the timeline):

1. \`rec-01/frames/03-0053.jpg\` · 0:05 · changed bottom-right (small), gone after 0.5 s — "Saving shows a toast that disappears fast."
2. \`rec-01/frames/04-0090.jpg\` · 0:09 · changed top-right (small) — "Look at the total, it says 1,240 but the line items add up to 1,180."
3. \`rec-01/frames/05-0160.jpg\` · 0:16 · changed top-right (small) · error at 0:16: TypeError: cannot read properties of undefined (reading "code") — "The coupon field still throws a validation error even with a valid code."
4. \`rec-01/frames/10-0295.jpg\` · 0:30 · most of the screen changed, final state — "And that's where it ends up."

**Contact sheets** show every keyframe, nine per image in time order, each tile captioned with its frame number and time. A magenta outline marks what changed since the tile before it; the frames themselves are untouched.

![0:00–0:27, frames 1–9](rec-01/grids/grid_01.jpg)

![0:30, frame 10](rec-01/grids/grid_02.jpg)

## Timeline

Each spoken line sits at its stamp, where the speaker started; the second time is where they stopped. → names the frame that best shows it, when that isn't the frame just above.

- **0:00** \`rec-01/frames/01-0000.jpg\` first frame
  > **0:01–0:03** This is the checkout page for a single order.
- **0:03** \`rec-01/frames/02-0030.jpg\` most of the screen changed
  > **0:05–0:06** Saving shows a toast that disappears fast. → \`rec-01/frames/03-0053.jpg\`
- **0:05** \`rec-01/frames/03-0053.jpg\` ★ changed bottom-right (small), gone after 0.5 s
  > **0:08–0:11** Look at the total, it says 1,240 but the line items add up to 1,180. → \`rec-01/frames/04-0090.jpg\`
- **0:09** \`rec-01/frames/04-0090.jpg\` ★ changed top-right (small)
  > **0:16–0:18** The coupon field still throws a validation error even with a valid code. → \`rec-01/frames/05-0160.jpg\`
- **0:16** \`rec-01/frames/05-0160.jpg\` ★ changed top-right (small)
  - \`[error] @ 0:16\` TypeError: cannot read properties of undefined (reading "code")
- **0:19** \`rec-01/frames/06-0190.jpg\` most of the screen changed
  > **0:19–0:21** The shipping modal opens fine.
- **0:22** \`rec-01/frames/07-0220.jpg\` changed center (small)
- **0:24** \`rec-01/frames/08-0240.jpg\` changed down the center
  > **0:27–0:29** Hovering the info icon shows a tooltip. → \`rec-01/frames/09-0273.jpg\`
